this has proven to be the end of the road,

3
00:02:37,017 --> 00:02:39,017
a graveyard of dreams.

4
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:44,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,017 --> 00:02:46,017
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,017 --> 00:02:49,017
sets sail into the new world with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:49,017 --> 00:02:53,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:56,017 --> 00:02:58,017
The first stop on Luffy's journey to the new world

9
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:00,017
is Fishman Island.

10
00:03:00,017 --> 00:03:02,017
Thousands of feet below sea level,

11
00:03:02,017 --> 00:03:05,017
where his crew becomes involved in a civil war.

12
00:03:05,017 --> 00:03:07,017
Meeting Jinbei in the sea forest,

13
00:03:07,017 --> 00:03:10,017
they learn of the events that led to the conflict.

14
00:03:10,017 --> 00:03:12,017
He tells the tale of the Fishman pilots,

15
00:03:12,017 --> 00:03:14,017
the island's brave queen,

16
00:03:14,017 --> 00:03:17,017
and its hero, Fisher Tiger.

17
00:03:24,017 --> 00:03:25,017
Back to the present.

18
00:03:25,017 --> 00:03:27,017
Horty makes a move.

19
00:03:30,017 --> 00:03:31,017
hunt' hours.

20
00:03:31,017 --> 00:03:36,017
には

21
00:03:36,017 --> 00:03:37,017
フローマン

22
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:39,017
エ Whoops!

23
00:03:39,017 --> 00:03:40,017
shipping

24
00:03:40,017 --> 00:03:41,017
には

25
00:03:41,017 --> 00:03:42,017
が

26
00:03:42,017 --> 00:03:42,717
犯人が

27
00:03:44,017 --> 00:03:46,017
唯一の猫に

28
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,297
ない死

29
00:03:48,397 --> 00:03:50,037
に

30
00:03:50,037 --> 00:03:52,017
残り

31
00:03:52,017 --> 00:04:12,657
Wait, Jinbei!

32
00:04:12,757 --> 00:04:14,777
What kind of scum would assassinate our queen?

33
00:04:16,117 --> 00:04:17,537
Spread out and find them!

34
00:04:17,997 --> 00:04:20,037
Turn the island upside down if you have to!

35
00:04:20,037 --> 00:04:24,897
First brother Tai, now Queen Otohime!

36
00:04:25,637 --> 00:04:27,937
I can't! I can't!

37
00:04:35,197 --> 00:04:37,697
How am I supposed to live with this anger?

38
00:04:38,337 --> 00:04:40,337
What piece could I ever hope to find?

39
00:04:42,817 --> 00:04:44,717
No, damn it!

40
00:04:45,057 --> 00:04:47,557
There he is! The shooter's up there!

41
00:04:48,097 --> 00:04:49,417
Go! Get to the rooftop!

42
00:04:50,037 --> 00:04:55,077
Is he the one?

43
00:04:56,097 --> 00:04:59,417
I saw him with a gun in his hand. There's no doubt.

44
00:05:01,457 --> 00:05:02,697
Where is the car?

45
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:05,917
Boss Jinbei! One of our men just killed him, sir.

46
00:05:06,117 --> 00:05:07,297
Was it someone we know?

47
00:05:07,837 --> 00:05:08,757
Far from it.

48
00:05:08,757 --> 00:05:14,077
It can't be!

49
00:05:14,077 --> 00:05:17,817
It's a human!

50
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:23,317
Hide the body!

51
00:05:23,977 --> 00:05:25,177
Hold on. Do what?

52
00:05:25,177 --> 00:05:31,997
If this gets out, it'll ruin everything the queen has accomplished.

53
00:05:32,997 --> 00:05:35,557
All of her work will be for nothing.

54
00:05:35,557 --> 00:05:38,517
She'll never be able to rest in peace!

55
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:44,677
Maybe. But that still doesn't change the truth, does it?

56
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:46,797
The truth is that he was a lawless pirate.

57
00:05:47,797 --> 00:05:50,997
Pirate or no pirate, all that matters is he was human.

58
00:05:51,137 --> 00:05:51,397
Huh?

59
00:05:52,297 --> 00:05:53,397
Leave it be, Horny!

60
00:05:54,057 --> 00:05:55,637
Don't do it, damn you!

61
00:05:55,637 --> 00:06:01,017
Listen, everyone!

62
00:06:01,017 --> 00:06:06,177
It was a human!

63
00:06:07,177 --> 00:06:11,357
A human assassinated our queen!

64
00:06:12,477 --> 00:06:15,697
This is what humans are capable of!

65
00:06:15,697 --> 00:06:19,197
Killing and co-blood!

66
00:06:26,077 --> 00:06:28,317
She trusted them with all her heart!

67
00:06:30,317 --> 00:06:31,417
A human?

68
00:06:32,237 --> 00:06:35,157
All she ever wanted was a peaceful coexistence.

69
00:06:35,497 --> 00:06:39,937
And this human murders her just when she finally had us convinced.

70
00:06:40,397 --> 00:06:42,937
We put all of our faith in her.

71
00:06:42,937 --> 00:06:47,757
And he's stolen that from us by taking Queen Otehime's life.

72
00:06:48,057 --> 00:06:51,257
He's taken our hearts and the future of this country.

73
00:06:51,777 --> 00:06:56,057
We could kill you a million times and never replace our queen, you human!

74
00:06:56,577 --> 00:06:58,577
Is there no justice in the world?

75
00:06:59,177 --> 00:07:00,957
What joy can we find now?

76
00:07:02,077 --> 00:07:03,537
It's more than I can take!

77
00:07:04,117 --> 00:07:06,237
All I can see is despair.

78
00:07:06,577 --> 00:07:08,257
All I can see is regret.

79
00:07:12,937 --> 00:07:24,297
Has the king agreed to leave the tower yet?

80
00:07:25,297 --> 00:07:26,377
Afraid not.

81
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,637
There's no reasoning with him.

82
00:07:30,237 --> 00:07:33,517
He's so stricken with grief and rage, he's lost all control.

83
00:07:33,517 --> 00:07:38,217
King Neptune!

84
00:07:38,217 --> 00:07:44,897
Lock the door behind me and leave it shut until my urge to kill has subsided!

85
00:07:44,897 --> 00:08:09,137
King Neptune, will you talk to me?

86
00:08:09,857 --> 00:08:10,317
Hmm?

87
00:08:10,957 --> 00:08:12,117
I'm listening.

88
00:08:12,917 --> 00:08:19,717
The shooter was discovered with the gun still in his hand, so one of our soldiers killed him.

89
00:08:20,537 --> 00:08:21,637
He was a human.

90
00:08:23,157 --> 00:08:27,277
I would have torn off his limbs whether he were armed or not.

91
00:08:27,277 --> 00:08:33,417
but my queen would never have allowed such savagery

92
00:08:33,417 --> 00:08:41,417
i don't even know when this all began but i would only perpetuate it further by seeking revenge

93
00:08:41,417 --> 00:08:47,537
if the children of our nation were to see me engage in such acts it would only teach them

94
00:08:47,537 --> 00:08:54,737
bitterness show them that rage is the answer and this horrible bloodshed would spiral onward

95
00:08:54,737 --> 00:09:02,097
it was easy to empathize with otohime's message of peace so long as it was someone else's problem

96
00:09:02,097 --> 00:09:09,017
but now why would it be wrong for me to kill the man who shot my wife to death

97
00:09:09,017 --> 00:09:16,377
why is that not my right as much as i want to i just can't understand that

98
00:09:16,377 --> 00:09:23,377
in my time as a soldier i took many lives in reprisal from my fallen comrades

99
00:09:23,377 --> 00:09:28,037
and i've killed swarms of humans over the years who besieged us

100
00:09:28,037 --> 00:09:33,057
but my hypocrisy kept me from helping otohime and her endeavors

101
00:09:33,057 --> 00:09:35,977
so i simply stood by her side and watched

102
00:09:35,977 --> 00:09:41,997
why should she die while a beast like me is allowed to live

103
00:09:41,997 --> 00:09:50,157
i could never take over her work because my hands are forever stained with the blood of my brutal history

104
00:09:50,157 --> 00:09:56,857
my king we're all teeming with contradictions and we all change with age

105
00:09:56,857 --> 00:09:59,357
that goes for fish men and humans alike

106
00:09:59,357 --> 00:10:05,277
but there are some things that only a soldier can have the strength to understand

107
00:10:05,277 --> 00:10:14,557
king neptune

108
00:10:14,557 --> 00:10:23,677
thank you for helping me i'm not certain if i'm ready but

109
00:10:23,677 --> 00:10:26,557
at least i can attend my wife's funeral

110
00:10:26,557 --> 00:10:31,997
father you made it i've missed you so much

111
00:10:31,997 --> 00:10:33,037
she's a hoshi

112
00:10:33,037 --> 00:10:42,017
father

113
00:10:42,017 --> 00:10:45,417
my brave sons

114
00:10:45,417 --> 00:10:46,957
welcome back

115
00:10:46,957 --> 00:10:56,957
i'm sorry children i shouldn't have left you alone during such a terrible time

116
00:10:56,957 --> 00:10:59,577
you should see this father

117
00:10:59,577 --> 00:11:00,857
hmm

118
00:11:00,857 --> 00:11:02,897
what is it

119
00:11:02,897 --> 00:11:06,417
these letters keep flying after me no matter where i go

120
00:11:06,417 --> 00:11:09,257
she's already received five of them father

121
00:11:09,257 --> 00:11:11,257
is this

122
00:11:11,257 --> 00:11:13,457
a love letter

123
00:11:13,457 --> 00:11:15,917
shira hos is only six years old

124
00:11:15,917 --> 00:11:18,597
who in blazes is this vander deccan

125
00:11:18,597 --> 00:11:21,737
that's the name of a legendary pirate isn't it sire

126
00:11:21,737 --> 00:11:26,877
my children will not attend the funeral

127
00:11:26,877 --> 00:11:30,977
there could be an accomplice still on the loose for all we know

128
00:11:30,977 --> 00:11:35,877
also i want this sleazy deccan character apprehended post haste

129
00:11:35,877 --> 00:11:36,637
yes sir

130
00:11:36,637 --> 00:11:39,117
oh

131
00:11:51,257 --> 00:11:53,077
oh

132
00:11:53,077 --> 00:11:53,317
oh

133
00:11:53,317 --> 00:11:55,057
oh

134
00:11:58,057 --> 00:11:58,477
oh

135
00:11:59,157 --> 00:12:01,057
oh

136
00:12:02,997 --> 00:12:04,997
oh

137
00:12:04,997 --> 00:12:05,837
oh

138
00:12:05,837 --> 00:12:16,497
My kingdom.

139
00:12:17,697 --> 00:12:18,997
Look up there.

140
00:12:21,817 --> 00:12:23,377
Prince Fukuboshi.

141
00:12:23,857 --> 00:12:24,917
Then he isn't here?

142
00:12:26,157 --> 00:12:26,877
Fukuboshi.

143
00:12:32,617 --> 00:12:34,777
To all my fellow fishmen.

144
00:12:36,717 --> 00:12:41,537
I'm sorry to interrupt my mother's funeral, but there's something I need to tell you.

145
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:46,497
So I ask that you please forgive me and lend me your full attention.

146
00:12:47,837 --> 00:12:52,937
In her last moment of life, my mother happily spoke to us of the future.

147
00:12:54,157 --> 00:12:56,377
She told us that we are almost there.

148
00:12:56,877 --> 00:12:58,957
Our new home in the light of the sun.

149
00:12:59,477 --> 00:13:04,037
We have chosen to adopt our mother's dream and dedicate our lives to seeing it through,

150
00:13:04,037 --> 00:13:05,937
no matter how long it takes.

151
00:13:07,197 --> 00:13:08,117
So noble.

152
00:13:08,917 --> 00:13:15,117
We understand that you are not yet ready, and you likely won't be, for the World Summit in two years.

153
00:13:15,917 --> 00:13:19,797
But there will be another in six years, and another after that in ten.

154
00:13:19,797 --> 00:13:26,137
It's only natural for this tragedy to have reaffirmed your deeply held mistrust of humans.

155
00:13:26,957 --> 00:13:30,697
So I'll destroy the remaining signatures that were left unburned.

156
00:13:30,697 --> 00:13:37,197
And together, we'll start from the beginning.

157
00:13:39,037 --> 00:13:43,497
Someday in our future, when your wounds have finally begun to heal,

158
00:13:43,577 --> 00:13:46,217
once you feel you are ready,

159
00:13:47,657 --> 00:13:53,377
united, we will dream of a new life in the sun.

160
00:13:53,377 --> 00:14:22,797
In the decade that followed,

161
00:14:22,797 --> 00:14:26,617
the remaining members of the royal family, including the king himself,

162
00:14:26,797 --> 00:14:31,077
rarely left the palace, but chose to speak to the nation through their monitors instead.

163
00:14:32,597 --> 00:14:36,457
And all the while, the islander's signature steadily replenished.

164
00:14:37,577 --> 00:14:38,957
So there you have it.

165
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:42,517
That's how we spent the past 16 years fighting discrimination.

166
00:14:43,577 --> 00:14:45,777
And that's how the Fishman Pirates were formed.

167
00:14:46,277 --> 00:14:46,997
And divided.

168
00:14:46,997 --> 00:14:53,317
There's no denying the awful things Arlong did to your home.

169
00:14:54,237 --> 00:14:58,337
Even so, at one time, he was like a brother to me.

170
00:14:58,337 --> 00:15:05,337
When we received news of his violent actions,

171
00:15:05,577 --> 00:15:07,837
we took it upon ourselves to stop him.

172
00:15:08,297 --> 00:15:11,197
But he always managed to dodge any real consequence.

173
00:15:11,937 --> 00:15:16,197
He hid his actions from the Navy by bribing any soldiers that he came across.

174
00:15:16,197 --> 00:15:20,097
I let him live, and in failing to stop him,

175
00:15:20,217 --> 00:15:22,397
I too share the guilt for his crimes.

176
00:15:22,397 --> 00:15:31,297
And that's why, though it pains me, it's my fault.

177
00:15:35,637 --> 00:15:36,617
Oh yeah?

178
00:15:37,797 --> 00:15:40,777
If you're so sorry, kill yourself.

179
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:42,537
Sanji!

180
00:15:42,857 --> 00:15:44,057
Take responsibility.

181
00:15:45,117 --> 00:15:47,617
Pay with your life for the suffering that you caused her.

182
00:15:48,017 --> 00:15:48,697
Give her peace.

183
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:50,557
That's enough, Sanji.

184
00:15:51,397 --> 00:15:51,817
What?

185
00:15:52,057 --> 00:15:53,237
Are you serious, Nami?

186
00:15:53,497 --> 00:15:55,837
How could you excuse the things they did to you?

187
00:15:55,857 --> 00:15:57,717
I'll never excuse what Arlong did.

188
00:15:58,137 --> 00:15:58,797
But Jinbei?

189
00:15:59,197 --> 00:16:00,857
He never meant for anyone to get hurt.

190
00:16:01,137 --> 00:16:01,477
Wait.

191
00:16:01,737 --> 00:16:02,397
Are you sure?

192
00:16:05,917 --> 00:16:07,877
I will accept any punishment.

193
00:16:08,297 --> 00:16:10,477
If you wish for me to take my own life...

194
00:16:10,477 --> 00:16:10,937
Drop it.

195
00:16:12,837 --> 00:16:13,977
Look, it's okay.

196
00:16:14,517 --> 00:16:16,137
The only one I hate is Arlong.

197
00:16:18,697 --> 00:16:25,857
Believe me, I'm relieved to hear you're not the mastermind of the Arlong Pirates.

198
00:16:26,537 --> 00:16:29,477
And you're a friend of Luffy's, which tells me plenty about you.

199
00:16:30,477 --> 00:16:31,317
I won't lie.

200
00:16:31,977 --> 00:16:34,277
The Arlong Pirates made my life a living hell.

201
00:16:35,397 --> 00:16:39,037
But you know, if it wasn't for that nightmare, I never would have met my friends.

202
00:16:40,397 --> 00:16:43,257
That awful time made me who I am.

203
00:16:43,257 --> 00:16:48,177
I can't hate you just because you're a fish man.

204
00:16:49,597 --> 00:16:51,097
So you...

205
00:16:51,097 --> 00:16:53,577
You don't get to pity me just because of my past.

206
00:16:55,457 --> 00:16:57,057
I'm fine with my past.

207
00:16:57,537 --> 00:16:59,097
Because I'm happy in the present.

208
00:16:59,097 --> 00:17:06,297
It doesn't matter who did this to me.

209
00:17:07,297 --> 00:17:08,737
Don't become angry.

210
00:17:09,377 --> 00:17:10,897
Not on my behalf.

211
00:17:12,897 --> 00:17:15,317
Please, you can't tell anyone on the island.

212
00:17:16,277 --> 00:17:17,837
The tragedy that we've endured.

213
00:17:18,377 --> 00:17:20,337
And our hatred must die with us.

214
00:17:20,337 --> 00:17:23,297
I wouldn't dwell on it.

215
00:17:23,457 --> 00:17:24,797
There's nothing you could have done.

216
00:17:25,137 --> 00:17:27,797
You've known each other since childhood, after all.

217
00:17:28,457 --> 00:17:30,797
Like him or not, he's still like a brother to you.

218
00:17:31,157 --> 00:17:32,017
And you're no killer.

219
00:17:32,017 --> 00:17:42,657
I don't deserve to be treated so kindly.

220
00:17:45,457 --> 00:17:47,237
You have my gratitude.

221
00:17:53,237 --> 00:17:53,637
Nami!

222
00:18:00,017 --> 00:18:01,697
You're a good man, Jinpei.

223
00:18:01,697 --> 00:18:06,577
I know how hard it is to be a big brother.

224
00:18:07,257 --> 00:18:09,177
You're a hell of a guy, Jinpei.

225
00:18:10,897 --> 00:18:12,257
That whole story.

226
00:18:12,677 --> 00:18:14,397
I like them all so much.

227
00:18:14,737 --> 00:18:16,677
Tiger and Odashime and what's his name?

228
00:18:16,677 --> 00:18:17,717
Shut your mouth, Frankie!

229
00:18:19,797 --> 00:18:22,257
He must have been carrying so much pain.

230
00:18:22,257 --> 00:18:32,937
Huh?

231
00:18:32,937 --> 00:18:32,957
Huh?

232
00:18:33,617 --> 00:18:34,037
Luffy?

233
00:18:34,037 --> 00:18:34,157
Luffy?

234
00:18:38,237 --> 00:18:38,837
What?

235
00:18:41,517 --> 00:18:42,037
Moron!

236
00:18:42,497 --> 00:18:43,197
Wake up!

237
00:18:43,197 --> 00:18:48,537
I needed that nap.

238
00:18:48,537 --> 00:18:49,317
I should have known.

239
00:18:49,957 --> 00:18:52,717
The only time you can sit still is if you're asleep.

240
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:53,477
Huh?

241
00:18:54,477 --> 00:18:54,977
Huh?

242
00:18:54,977 --> 00:18:57,117
Jinbei, are you crying?

243
00:18:57,717 --> 00:18:57,957
Huh?

244
00:18:58,717 --> 00:18:59,797
Oh, come now.

245
00:18:59,857 --> 00:19:01,917
Of course I'm not crying.

246
00:19:01,917 --> 00:19:04,717
What did I miss?

247
00:19:04,877 --> 00:19:06,057
It's nothing, all right?

248
00:19:06,297 --> 00:19:07,037
Let's forget it.

249
00:19:07,137 --> 00:19:07,937
Move on.

250
00:19:08,817 --> 00:19:09,137
Hmm.

251
00:19:10,037 --> 00:19:10,477
Sure.

252
00:19:10,837 --> 00:19:11,237
Whatever.

253
00:19:12,597 --> 00:19:16,817
So, Jinbei, what did the queen end up doing to that thief she got?

254
00:19:17,337 --> 00:19:18,477
Are you for real?

255
00:19:18,477 --> 00:19:21,257
You mean you fell asleep at the very beginning of the story?

256
00:19:21,397 --> 00:19:22,197
Did I miss it all?

257
00:19:22,257 --> 00:19:22,857
You did!

258
00:19:23,797 --> 00:19:24,997
Shirohoshi, right?

259
00:19:25,637 --> 00:19:26,437
You gonna be okay?

260
00:19:27,797 --> 00:19:28,317
Namichin!

261
00:19:28,537 --> 00:19:29,397
She's royalty!

262
00:19:29,697 --> 00:19:31,317
Don't be so casual, please!

263
00:19:31,717 --> 00:19:34,677
Oh, forgive me for being so emotional.

264
00:19:35,377 --> 00:19:37,997
It's difficult not to cry when I think about my mother.

265
00:19:38,897 --> 00:19:40,597
She sounds like she was quite the woman.

266
00:19:42,697 --> 00:19:43,137
Yes.

267
00:19:44,837 --> 00:19:47,097
It's a real pleasure to meet you, Namichin.

268
00:19:47,097 --> 00:19:48,797
No, princess.

269
00:19:49,237 --> 00:19:52,997
Namichin is just a silly nickname I gave her, so it's just plain Nami.

270
00:19:53,217 --> 00:19:53,717
No, Jin!

271
00:19:53,837 --> 00:19:54,617
Excuse me.

272
00:19:55,037 --> 00:19:57,177
Perhaps it's a bit forward of me to say this,

273
00:19:57,537 --> 00:20:00,137
but even though we just met, I feel a connection to you.

274
00:20:00,497 --> 00:20:02,497
Like we've been friends for a long time.

275
00:20:02,937 --> 00:20:03,377
Oh, yeah?

276
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:06,557
Well, we've both been through some similar rough patches.

277
00:20:11,937 --> 00:20:12,957
Excuse me.

278
00:20:14,157 --> 00:20:16,117
I just lost track of time.

279
00:20:16,117 --> 00:20:19,797
I need to know what the situation is at the Ryugu Palace.

280
00:20:20,317 --> 00:20:22,337
Just to confirm what you've told me,

281
00:20:22,537 --> 00:20:25,677
Horty and his crew have taken the king and the palace guards captive.

282
00:20:26,357 --> 00:20:29,977
Apart from that, you're not sure what happened to three members of your crew.

283
00:20:30,757 --> 00:20:32,977
And that's all the information we have, correct?

284
00:20:32,977 --> 00:20:34,237
You...

285
00:20:34,237 --> 00:20:35,177
Hey, Jinbei!

286
00:20:35,757 --> 00:20:38,237
If the siege is playing out as Horty planned,

287
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:42,477
there's a good chance the rest of the country is falling to his forces now, too.

288
00:20:43,537 --> 00:20:44,417
Hold on.

289
00:20:44,797 --> 00:20:46,837
Are you saying you know what his plan is?

290
00:20:47,277 --> 00:20:53,237
To be honest, I have had my suspicions he was up to something ever since he retired from the army.

291
00:20:53,237 --> 00:20:56,857
But he was clever enough to keep the details hidden from me.

292
00:20:56,857 --> 00:20:58,777
Not me.

293
00:20:59,017 --> 00:20:59,657
I know.

294
00:21:00,237 --> 00:21:01,897
But first, let me warn you.

295
00:21:02,317 --> 00:21:04,777
Horty hates humans even more than Arlong did.

296
00:21:05,317 --> 00:21:07,397
The only thing driving him is resentment.

297
00:21:07,817 --> 00:21:12,197
He talks about rebuilding the kingdom, but all he really wants to do is cause suffering to humans.

298
00:21:12,197 --> 00:21:17,797
And to prove my point, you'll see there's one big difference between him and Arlong.

299
00:21:18,797 --> 00:21:24,097
Arlong had no problem with killing humans, but the one thing he'd never do is hurt other fishmen.

300
00:21:25,557 --> 00:21:27,297
Horty, he doesn't care.

301
00:21:28,117 --> 00:21:31,717
He'll also turn his fury against fishmen who are sympathetic to humans.

302
00:21:32,597 --> 00:21:34,897
He'll cut down anyone in his way.

303
00:21:35,777 --> 00:21:40,777
The World Summit is set to take place again soon, but a lot's changed in the last four years.

304
00:21:40,777 --> 00:21:51,077
For the first time since Odohime's death, they've actually gathered enough signatures for King Neptune to speak at the summit about relocating Fishman Island to the surface.

305
00:21:52,257 --> 00:21:54,517
Hmm. I see.

306
00:21:55,377 --> 00:21:57,817
Then Horty has seized the palace just for that?

307
00:21:57,917 --> 00:21:58,497
I wish.

308
00:21:59,077 --> 00:22:01,237
No, I'm afraid it's a lot worse than that.

309
00:22:05,977 --> 00:22:06,577
Ah!

310
00:22:07,717 --> 00:22:09,657
What? What is that?

311
00:22:10,777 --> 00:22:15,257
It's huge! They get that big?

312
00:22:15,997 --> 00:22:20,857
What the? It's a video transponder snail. What's it doing out here?

313
00:22:23,537 --> 00:22:25,317
Look! It's activated!

314
00:22:26,317 --> 00:22:29,237
Oh yeah, it's projecting! On the bubble!

315
00:22:29,777 --> 00:22:30,537
Ah!

316
00:22:31,537 --> 00:22:33,537
Hmm. I thought so.

317
00:22:33,537 --> 00:22:34,757
It's him.

318
00:22:34,757 --> 00:22:39,077
What's up?

319
00:22:40,077 --> 00:22:40,857
You know that guy?

320
00:22:41,497 --> 00:22:42,257
That's Horty.

321
00:22:42,937 --> 00:22:44,037
This can't be good.

322
00:22:45,397 --> 00:22:46,357
He found us?

323
00:22:46,617 --> 00:22:47,197
Hodgins!

324
00:22:47,197 --> 00:22:51,417
Hello there, people of Fishman Island.

325
00:22:51,417 --> 00:22:53,917
Am I coming through?

326
00:22:53,917 --> 00:23:00,677
Well then, for those of you who don't know, I'm the captain of the new Fishman Pirates.

327
00:23:00,677 --> 00:23:05,057
My name is Horty Jones!

328
00:23:05,057 --> 00:23:06,277
I'm the captain of the new Fishman Pirates.

329
00:23:06,277 --> 00:23:07,977
I'm the captain of the new Fishman Pirates.

330
00:23:08,277 --> 00:23:13,237
Broadcasting across all of Fishman Island, Horty makes his plans for conquest clear.

331
00:23:13,677 --> 00:23:17,277
The people watch in horror as he prepares for Neptune's execution.

332
00:23:17,957 --> 00:23:22,037
Those who would oppose him are scattered across the island with his straw hats in disarray.

333
00:23:22,497 --> 00:23:26,197
Luffy is ready to fight, but Jinbei has something else in mind.

334
00:23:26,197 --> 00:23:33,937
on the next wood piece the kingdom in shock an order to execute neptune issued i'm gonna be king

335
00:23:33,937 --> 00:23:34,817
of the pirates

